WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.495
The method has two parts.

00:00:01.575 --> 00:00:03.384
To kill the finite-nudge bias,

00:00:03.464 --> 00:00:08.927
the authors build on holomorphic EP: they drive the
network with an oscillating teaching

00:00:09.007 --> 00:00:14.533
signal and use a Cauchy integral from complex
analysis to recover the exact error vector,

00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:19.005
no matter how large the nudge and even when the
Jacobian is asymmetric.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:23.918
Better still, this can be estimated continuously
over many oscillation cycles,

00:00:23.998 --> 00:00:27.319
removing the need for separate free and nudged phases.

00:00:27.399 --> 00:00:28.956
To tackle the second bias,

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:32.987
they show it grows with the skew-symmetric part of
the Jacobian,

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:37.145
and introduce a homeostatic loss that penalizes
exactly that part,

00:00:37.225 --> 00:00:40.546
estimated efficiently with the Hutchinson trace trick.

00:00:40.626 --> 00:00:45.963
The key insight is that this improves functional
symmetry of the Jacobian without ever

00:00:46.043 --> 00:00:48.230
forcing the weights to be symmetric.
